Saved unit_heterogeneity_agentB_B_then_A_generalist_withGAE_PPO_phase2_seed3_fixedB_neuralsubset.pdf

--- How to read this ---
If ~half the units dip and ~half rise (like a coin flip), and no small
subset dominates: the population-mean dip is a WEAK/borderline summary,
not strong evidence of coordinated suppression -- individual units are
doing different things that happen to net out slightly negative.
If the large majority of units genuinely dip, and the effect isn't just
a few outliers: that's real evidence of a shared, coordinated signal at
the moment of the pull decision.
  (partner_force is constant in this eval for agent A -- can't correlate, all NaN)
